# The Myth of the First Echo

In the time before time, when the world was newly formed, Sound was a lonely spirit who wandered the earth seeking companionship. Wherever Sound traveled, her voice would fade into the void, never to return.

One day, Sound came upon a great mountain sleeping beneath the stars. In her loneliness, she sang the most beautiful melody ever created—a song of longing and hope. As her notes drifted toward the mountain, something miraculous happened.

The mountain, moved by her melody, awakened and sang back to her. But the mountain could not create its own song, so it did the next best thing: it returned Sound's melody to her, slightly softer, slightly changed by the mountain's stony heart.

Sound was overjoyed. For the first time, she was not alone. She sang again, and again the mountain returned her voice. They continued this way through the night, creating the world's first conversation.

From that day forward, Sound blessed all mountains, valleys, and caves with the gift of Echo—the ability to return voices to those who call out. And so, whenever we hear our echo, we remember Sound's gift: that no voice should ever be truly alone.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

